'''Jewels''' are items that can be placed into allocated [[jewel socket]]s in the [[passive skill tree]], and can be removed or replaced at no cost. They grant certain buffs and abilities. Like most other items, jewels can be modified by orbs and are available in the four rarities. A rare jewel can have only four affixes instead of six.

It is possible to have a jewel in an unallocated slot. Jewels in unallocated slots have no effect <ref>Using the full respec granted by update, I removed all skills, leaving jewels in slots. Those supposed to increase attributes (easy to verify) didn't do so.</ref>.

Some [[List of unique jewels|unique jewels]] affect other passive nodes within a certain [[Jewel#Radius|radius]].

[[Abyss jewel]]s are special types of jewels that can be socketed into jewel sockets as well as abyssal socket in items. [[Cluster jewel]]s can only be socketed in the outermost jewel sockets and adds a passive skill cluster to the passive tree.

==Base Jewels==
There are three base jewel types. They don't differ in implicit modifiers or level requirement, but rather in the pool of modifiers that can spawn on them. 
Jewels can be found starting at item level 20, and used at any level.

* {{il|Cobalt Jewel}}
* {{il|Crimson Jewel}}
* {{il|Viridian Jewel}}

Only magic, rare, and unique jewels can be found in loot. Normal jewels can be obtained by using an {{il|Orb of Scouring}}.

There is a fourth base type, {{il|Prismatic Jewel}}, which can only be found as a {{c|unique|[[unique]]}} item (and subsequently converted it to non-unique rarity). See its page for more information.

==Cluster Jewels==
{{main|Cluster Jewel}}
Cluster jewels can be found in [[Delirium]] encounters. Cluster jewels can only be socketed in the jewel sockets located at the outer-most part of the passive skill tree. They add a passive skill cluster to the passive tree when socketed. They have modifiers that determine how many and what skills are in the cluster. Larger cluster jewels can have jewel sockets, which can support smaller cluster jewels or any other types of jewels.

* {{il|Small Cluster Jewel}}
* {{il|Medium Cluster Jewel}}
* {{il|Large Cluster Jewel}}

Unlike regular jewels, cluster jewel mods are [[item level]] dependent.

==Abyss Jewels==
{{main|Abyss Jewel}}
Abyss jewels can be found as drops from an [[Abyss]]. They behave mostly like regular jewels, except that they can also be socketed into equipment with abyssal sockets. Abyss jewels frequently have modifiers that are not available on regular jewels.

* {{il|Ghastly Eye Jewel}}
* {{il|Hypnotic Eye Jewel}}
* {{il|Murderous Eye Jewel}}
* {{il|Searching Eye Jewel}}

Unlike regular jewels, abyss jewel mods are [[item level]] dependent.

There is a fifth base type, {{il|Assembled Eye Jewel}}, which can only be found as a {{c|unique|[[unique]]}} item (and subsequently converted it to non-unique rarity). See its page for more information.

==Unique jewels==
{{see also|List of unique jewels|Timeless Jewel|Threshold Jewel}}

There are several unique jewels. [[List of unique jewels received by drop|Some are dropped]] and others can be only be gained through [[List of unique jewels received by corruption|corrupting jewels]].[[File:Jewel screenshot.png|thumbnail|right|A jewel with a ''large'' radius]]

===Radius===
Some unique jewels may come with a radius in which a specific effect occurs. The radius modifier represents the following internal values:
{|class=wikitable
! Size || Radius || Radius (ring)
|-
| Small || 800 || 800-1100
|-
| Medium || 1200 || 1100-1400
|-
| Large || 1500 || 1400-1700
|-
| Very Large || 2000 || 1700-2000
|-
| Massive || 2400 || 2000-2400
|}

[[Mastery|Masteries]], passives created by [[cluster jewel]]s, and any passives not on the passive tree itself ([[Ascendancy class]] skills, [[Oils|Anoint]]-only passives) are not counted in any radius related jewel effects, even if it visually looks like it does. Similarly, jewels placed on jewels sockets from cluster jewels have their radius effects disabled.

===Passage Jewels===
'''Passage Jewels''' are a group unique jewels that allow allocation of passive skills that are not connected to the rest of the character's passives<ref>https://x.com/pathofexile/status/1983680626038616447</ref>. There are currently three Passage Jewels:

* {{il|Intuitive Leap}}
* {{il|page=Thread of Hope}} (small to very large) / {{il|page=Thread of Hope (Massive Ring)}} (massive)
* {{il|Impossible Escape}}

All Passage Jewels have the following restrictions:

* The jewel slot the Passage Jewel is socketed in must be connected to the tree. Jewels in unallocated jewel sockets are disabled.
* Passage Jewels' range effects do not function in [[cluster jewel]] sockets, and Passage Jewels cannot allocate passives added by a cluster jewel even if they are visually within range.
* Jewel sockets cannot be allocated using a Passage Jewel.
* [[Ascendancy class|Ascendancy passives]] and any other passive skills not part of the main passive skill tree cannot be allocated using a Passage Jewel.
* [[Mastery|Masteries]] cannot be allocated by allocating an unconnected notable passive.
* Singular passives allocated through a Passage Jewel's range are not considered connected to other passives, and are not able to connect to other passives outside of the jewel's range.
** It is still possible to connect the passive if it is directly connected to from the rest of the character's passives.
* A Passage Jewel cannot be removed from the jewel socket until all unconnected passives in range are refunded.

See also: {{il|Unnatural Instinct}}. While not a Passage Jewel, it is broadly similar, granting certain passives in its radius.

===Mycelium Core===
{{il|Putrid Seed}} has a special base jewel type. It can only be placed on Large Jewel Sockets. They work similarly to [[cluster jewel]]s and add new passive nodes, but instead of adding a cluster, it adds a branching path of passive nodes in a pattern that depends on which Large Jewel Socket it's placed in, though they all add the same total number of passives.

==Corrupted==
The [[corrupted]] property can have the following effects on a jewel:
* Turn into a rare jewel
* Turn into a Vaal-exclusive unique jewel with the same base item (see: [[list of unique jewels received by corruption]])
* Add an implicit modifier to the jewel
* No effect (other than adding the corrupted property)

==Affixes==
===Basic jewels===
Affixes for basic jewels follow some special rules:
* No item level requirement
* No tiered affixes
* Rare items can only roll 4 affixes, 2 prefixes and 2 suffixes each

